6:         pairingsPerPoint: 1
6:         threshold: 2.0*ADAPTIVE_THRESHOLD_SIGMA
6:         # Optional range-adaptive matching distance. thresholdFar: 0 (the
6:         # default) keeps the flat threshold above, i.e. today's behaviour
6:         # exactly. When set, the matching distance ramps from `threshold` near
6:         # the sensor to `thresholdFar` beyond `thresholdKneeRange`.
6:         # 
6:         # Why the axis exists: a pose-prediction error `dtheta` displaces a
6:         # point at range `r` by `dtheta*r`, so a flat threshold rejects far
6:         # returns first, precisely when the prediction is worst. Measured: at a
6:         # flat 0.34 m, 1 deg of yaw error takes beyond-25 m acceptance from 82%
6:         # to 4.6% while r<10 m stays at 99%; a 1.0 m far window keeps 94%. Those
6:         # far returns carry most of the rotation and along-track leverage.
6:         # 
6:         # Note this is a no-op while ADAPTIVE_THRESHOLD_SIGMA sits at its
